{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/9/codegen_prompts/1.md')\nprint(p.read_text()[:8000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/9`\n- 题号：`1`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/9/1.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"1\">\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内部的标记像素颜色，从色板行中选取对应颜色对该区域的边框进行重新上色，目标边框由色板段长度与边框周长的匹配决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格最底部一行是\"色板行\"：由若干段不同颜色的连续水平色块组成，每段色块长度不同，颜色互不相同，段与段之间用黑色像素分隔。\n  - 网格上方区域包含若干个用灰色（grey）像素绘制的封闭矩形边框（宽度为 1 像素），矩形之间互不重叠、互不接触。\n  - 每个灰色矩形内部恰好有一个非黑色、非灰色的单像素标记点，标记颜色与色板行中某一段色块的颜色相同。\n  - 色板行中每段色块的长度（像素数）各不相同，且恰好等于某个灰色矩形边框的周长像素数（周长 = 矩形边框上所有灰色像素的总数）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 对每个灰色矩形，读取其内部标记像素的颜色 C。\n  2. 在色板行中找到颜色为 C 的那一段色块，读取其长度 L。\n  3. 在所有灰色矩形中，找到边框周长像素数恰好等于 L 的那个矩形 T（T 与当前矩形可以是同一个，也可以不同）。\n  4. 将矩形 T 的灰色边框像素全部重新上色为 C。\n  5. 擦除所有标记像素（恢复为黑色背景）。色板行保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：标记颜色不是直接重绘自身矩形的边框，而是通过色板行建立\"颜色→长度→周长匹配\"的间接映射，将颜色传递到周长匹配的另一个矩形上。解题者需要先发现颜色-色板-长度的对应关系，再发现长度与目标矩形周长的匹配关系，这构成两层非显然的推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/88e364bc, train/e3fe1151, train/538b439f, train/e734a0e8, eval/89565ca0, eval/581f7754, eval/21897d95, train/2ccd9fef\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3016\nmechanism=0.3517\nlexical=0.0119\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:marker, object:rectangle, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e3fe